-# Latch/fork regime-key-mismatch incident — day_posture dead 2026-08-14 → 2026-08-20
-
-## Summary
-
-`day_posture._regime_snapshot` (day_posture.py:334-346) read `r.get("regime")`
-and `r.get("confidence")` off `regime_engine.latest_result()`. The engine's
-result cache is populated with `_telemetry_record()` (regime_engine.py:1669),
-whose keys are `winning_regime` / `confidence_final` — the legacy `"regime"` /
-`"confidence"` keys do not exist on the record. Every call fell through to
-the `CHOP` / `0.0` fallback, so `_apply_latch_transition` never observed a
-`STRONG_TREND_*` label and the `trend_confirmed` latch never SET via the
-regime path.
-
-Live-window scope: `bf73775` (2026-08-14, `feat(day_posture): shared posture
-helper + DAY_TIER_MASK + TREND_V3_UM`) shipped the reader. `1fca0eb`
-(2026-08-15) added the primer and range fork that consume the latch. Fixed
-by `ee18d63` (2026-08-20T11:47Z) — `winning_regime` / `confidence_final`
-substitution, plus a schema regression test that fails loudly on future
-renames (`tests/unit/test_day_posture_regime_snapshot_keys.py`).
-
-## Evidence — the latch never fired
-
-`grep -c "trend latch SET\|trend latch FLIPPED\|\[PRIMER\] fired"` across
-`logs/daily_journal.md` → `0` for both, from 2026-08-14 through 2026-08-20
-(pre-fix). Every `[RANGE-FORK] resolved` line in that window carried
-`resolved_by=no_trend_by_cutoff` regardless of what the market actually did.
-Verbatim daily counts from `logs/daily_journal.jsonl`:
-
-    2026-08-14  forks= 0  primer_fires= 0  latch_sets= 0
-    2026-08-15  forks= 0  primer_fires= 0  latch_sets= 0
-    2026-08-16  forks= 1  primer_fires= 0  latch_sets= 0
-    2026-08-17  forks= 2  primer_fires= 0  latch_sets= 0
-    2026-08-18  forks= 2  primer_fires= 0  latch_sets= 0
-    2026-08-19  forks= 0  primer_fires= 0  latch_sets= 0
-
-(Days without a fork line are days that ran BIG or MIDDLE — those subtypes
-skip the fork entirely; the primer would apply to MIDDLE / BIG-post-release,
-which also never fired.)
-
-## Corroborating case — 2026-08-20 GBPUSD
-
-Engine (`logs/regime_engine.jsonl`) classified `winning_regime=STRONG_TREND_UP`
-for GBPUSD continuously from `2026-08-20T08:05:00 → 11:20:00 UTC`
-(40 consecutive 5m bars, `regime_label_path=hist`, ADX 35→53, DI margin
-+25→+32, `EMA_state=BULL_ALIGNED`, `h1_macd_hist_slope` positive). Same
-process, same cache row read by `gbpusd_bb_bounce.py:2456` via
-`_rg.get("winning_regime")` — that reader correctly identified
-`STRONG_TREND_UP` and blocked SELL fades all morning. day_posture,
-reading `"regime"` off the same cache, saw `CHOP` the entire window.
-
-Consequence on 2026-08-20:
-
-- `cache/day_posture_latch.json` symbol_latch.GBPUSD held
-  `trend_confirmed=false, direction=null, confirmed_at_utc=null,
-  confirmed_by=null` all morning.
-- `[RANGE-FORK] resolved sym=GBPUSD subtype=POST_BIG range_mode=True
-  resolved_by=no_trend_by_cutoff cutoff=09:30` fired at 09:30:01Z
-  against a fresh-and-correct STRONG_TREND_UP tape.
-- Every `GBPUSD_TREND_V3_L BUY` fire attempt suppressed by
-  `DAY_TIER_MASK` (verbatim: `subtype_policy subtype=POST_BIG
-  range_mode=True trend_family_blocked mode_not_in_range_allowlist`
-  — reasoned pre-fork mask branch trade_executor.py:1513-1524).
-  Observed suppressions at 07:50 (STRUCTURE_BREAK_L),
-  09:35 / 10:15 / 10:20 (TREND_V3_L), all GBPUSD.
-- `[TREND_V3] FIRE LONG | ... regime=STRONG_TREND_UP ADX=53.3>=25.0
-  ER=0.51>=0.50 target=atr_fallback(13664.63) sl=12p tp=11p` at
-  10:20:01Z was authored by the strategy and then killed by the mask
-  in the very next line — the strategy read the regime correctly,
-  day_posture didn't, and the mask sided with day_posture.
-
-## Corpus poisoning window & re-derivation guidance
-
-Every signal_log / journal row whose `fire_ts` fell in
-`[2026-08-14T00:00:00 UTC, 2026-08-20T11:47Z]` and that carries
-posture-derived fields is contaminated. Specifically, these fields are wrong
-(or absent because a fire was blocked that shouldn't have been):
-
-- `posture.trend_confirmed`, `posture.latch_direction`,
-  `posture.latch_confirmed_by`, `posture.latch_confirmed_at_utc` —
-  will read False / None / None / None for every row.
-- `posture.range_mode`, `posture.range_fork_resolved_by`,
-  `posture.range_fork_resolved_at_utc` — for PRE_BIG / POST_BIG /
-  NORMAL subtypes the fork always resolves True / `no_trend_by_cutoff`
