-# Stale-pivot-anchor incident — 2026-08-19 D1 cache miss
-
-## Summary
-
-`cache/htf/GBPUSD_D1.json` and `cache/htf/EURUSD_D1.json` were not updated at
-the 2026-08-19T22:00 UTC FX-day boundary (root cause: runtime `d1_closed`
-cache-save silently swallowed to `logger.debug` — exact stack lost to journal
-rotation). Both files retained a mtime of `2026-08-19 14:52 UTC` (process
-preload) with tail bar `2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00` until manual repair at
-2026-08-20T10:48 UTC.
-
-Consequence: every D1-anchored feature computed on 2026-08-20 fires used the
-2026-08-18 bar (H=13553.9, L=13519.4, C=13533.4) instead of the
-2026-08-19 bar.
-
-## Canonical 2026-08-19 D1 bar (amendment, 2026-08-20 12:xx UTC)
-
-The manual repair at 2026-08-20T10:48 UTC wrote a tick-derived bar
-aggregated from the full 288-row CSV (00:00-23:55 UTC calendar day),
-producing H=13630.55 L=13523.25 C=13599.55. A subsequent autobot
-restart at ~12:xx UTC then triggered the runtime `d1_closed` save,
-overwriting the manual bar with the **process-fetched** value
-(the aggregator's own view of the FX-day window [Aug-18 22:00,
-Aug-19 22:00)) with H=13630.10 L=13522.80 C=13602.80.
-
-**Canonical bar (as of this amendment): H=13630.10 L=13522.80
-C=13602.80.** This is what `cache/htf/GBPUSD_D1.json` currently
-carries and what every downstream consumer now reads on the same
-file-per-eval load path (`bb_pd_gate._select_prior_d1` →
-`htf_cache.load_cached_candles`). Both value sets and the delta:
-
-| bar          | H        | L        | C        |
-| ------------ | -------- | -------- | -------- |
-| Manual repair | 13630.55 | 13523.25 | 13599.55 |
-| Canonical (process) | 13630.10 | 13522.80 | 13602.80 |
-| Delta        | −0.45p   | −0.45p   | **+3.25p** |
-
-The +3.25p on C shifts P from 13584.45 (manual) to 13585.23
-(canonical) — a +0.78p pivot shift. R1/R2/R3 shift by
-~+2.02p/+0.78p/+2.02p respectively (2026-08-20 verification math
-below). The delta is small enough that the qualitative
-misclassification story below is unchanged, but the exact numbers
-downstream (bbc_*, PIVOT-GATE, PIVOT_BREAK) must be re-computed
-against the canonical bar for corpus purposes.
-
-The manual repair remained in the cache for ~1h30m (10:48-12:xx
-UTC). Any signal_log rows opened in that window carry pivots
-derived from the manual bar; rows opened after ~12:xx UTC (and
-subsequent fires forever after) carry pivots derived from the
-canonical bar. Both are valid — the manual repair fixed the
-zero-bar cache miss (fires between 00:00-10:48 UTC would otherwise
-have used the 2026-08-18 bar as prior); the canonical bar is the
-process's own reading of the FX-day window and is what corpus
-studies should use as ground truth going forward.
-
-## Affected pairs
-
-- GBPUSD  — cache tail 2026-08-18 → repaired to (manual, tick-derived)
-  O=13535.95 H=13630.55 L=13523.25 C=13599.55 (aggregated from
-  `/opt/tradingbot/data/candles/GBPUSD/2026-08-19.csv`, 288 5-min rows,
-  full calendar-day window), then overwritten at ~12:xx UTC by the
-  process's own d1_closed save with **canonical (process-fetched)**
-  H=13630.10 L=13522.80 C=13602.80. See "Canonical 2026-08-19 D1 bar"
-  section above.
