-## Source-convention amendment (2026-08-21 12:xx UTC restart, 20-Aug bar)
-
-**Convention:** IG API D1 bar values (fetched by the runtime preload /
-gap-fill via `htf_cache._apply_d1_writer_guard`) are **canonical**.
-Archive-built repair bars — tick-CSV aggregations written by manual
-repair scripts — are **emergency bridges** that live only until the
-next preload or FX-day boundary refresh overwrites them. Re-repairing
-back to the archive values will just be undone at the next
-preload/boundary; don't chase it.
-
-**Why the uniform ±0.45p/±0.30p H and L delta looks like corruption
-but isn't:** archive tick aggregation builds bars from the **bid**
-feed; the IG API DAY bar is IG's own snapshot (closer to mid, or
-their own H/L extremum bookkeeping that differs by a fixed
-half-spread offset per symbol). The delta shows up as the same
-signed offset on H **and** L within a symbol — a translation, not
-a range distortion. That signature (H and L moved by identical
-amounts) is the diagnostic: uniform H/L shift ⇒ source-convention
-diff ⇒ not corruption. A real corruption event would move H, L, O,
-C incoherently.
-
-**Today's 20-Aug bar — before/after the 12:02 restart preload:**
-
-GBPUSD:
-
-| bar                         | O        | H        | L        | C        |
-| --------------------------- | -------- | -------- | -------- | -------- |
-| Archive repair (11:13 UTC)  | 13606.35 | 13659.85 | 13594.95 | 13631.55 |
-| Canonical / IG API (12:02)  | 13602.90 | 13659.40 | 13594.50 | 13635.40 |
-| Delta                       | −3.45p   | −0.45p   | −0.45p   | +3.85p   |
-
-EURUSD:
-
-| bar                         | O        | H        | L        | C        |
-| --------------------------- | -------- | -------- | -------- | -------- |
-| Archive repair (11:13 UTC)  | 11675.55 | 11710.70 | 11669.60 | 11678.35 |
-| Canonical / IG API (12:02)  | 11674.50 | 11710.40 | 11669.30 | 11682.80 |
-| Delta                       | −1.05p   | −0.30p   | −0.30p   | +4.45p   |
-
-H and L move by identical amounts per symbol (−0.45p GBPUSD, −0.30p
-EURUSD) — the bid-vs-IG-DAY half-spread signature. O and C differ
-more because the archive aggregation defines them from the first/last
-tick of the calendar-day CSV window, while the IG DAY bar defines
-them from the FX-day window (D-1 22:00 → D 22:00 UTC). Same ruling
