-## C2 rejection-shape tightening — evaluated and rejected (2026-08-21)
-
-Two variants of a LEVEL_BOUNCE C2-tightening were evaluated in
-response to the four overnight phantom fires (2026-08-21 00:10 / 00:30
-/ 01:45 / 03:00 SELL against R1=13647.67) and both rejected on replay
-evidence. Recorded here so the same ideas aren't re-proposed in October.
-
-**Variant 1 — cleared-level check.** Refuse fire if any 5m bar since
-current FX-day open (22:00 UTC) closed beyond level by ≥ 5p in the
-opposing direction. Replay of all 16 LEVEL_BOUNCE fires: catches
-only 1 of the 4 overnight phantom fires (03:00, because 02:45 close
-= 13654.35 crossed R1+5=13652.66); the first three phantom fires had
-no pre-fire close beyond R1+5 within the current FX day. Also kills
-the 2026-08-20T13:15 SELL winner (+12.45p) — a 10:05 UTC bar closed
-at 13652.75 above R1+5 within the FX day. Net PnL delta on the sample
-≈ −5p. Rejected.
-
-**Variant 2 — C2 depth ≥ 2p + close in outer third of C2's range.**
-Twin of `level_ladder._is_rejection_at_rung` (rung → BB band). Replay
-of the 5 fires with local 5m coverage (2026-08-19T22:00 onward — deep
-CSV is stuck at 2026-03; rolling holds ~48h):
-
-| fire                | C2 depth | outer-3rd | verdict | actual pnl |
-| ------------------- | -------- | --------- | ------- | ---------- |
-| 2026-08-20 13:15 W  | 1.15p    | true      | REFUSE  | +12.45     |
-| 2026-08-21 00:10 L  | 2.32p    | true      | PASS    |  −6.70     |
-| 2026-08-21 00:30 L  | 1.15p    | true      | REFUSE  |  −7.60     |
-| 2026-08-21 01:45 L  | 3.37p    | true      | PASS    |  −7.10     |
-| 2026-08-21 03:00 L  | 0.09p    | true      | REFUSE  |  −7.40     |
-
-Kills 1 winner. Refuses only 2 of 4 phantom fires — the other two
-(00:10, 01:45) had C2 depth 2.32p and 3.37p, well above threshold —
-so the "they were shallow wobbles" premise held for only 2 of 4.
-All 5 fires had bottom-third close, so the outer-third element added
-no discrimination on this sample. No clean threshold separates the
-winner (1.15p depth) from the 00:30 phantom loser (1.15p depth) —
-they are identical on the geometry the check inspects. Rejected;
-threshold-tuning to force a pass was explicitly forbidden.
-
-Ruling: **the staleness gate (`LEVEL_BOUNCE_REFUSE_STALE_ANCHOR=1`,
-shipped this morning) is the complete defence for the phantom-anchor
-class.** The C2 rejection shape of the overnight fires was sound —
-close back inside band, close in the outer third. What made the fires
-phantom was the stale D1 anchor producing a pivot value the market
-had already left behind, and the staleness gate refuses the whole
-class before C2 even matters. Adding a C2-shape filter is redundant
-at best (catching a strict subset the staleness gate already caught)
-and destructive at worst (killing a same-shape winner on fresh
-anchors).
-
-**Correction to the "fresh anchor" claim.** The 2026-08-20T13:15
-replay report described the anchor as FRESH. That's true by the
-gap-days rule — 20-Aug (Thursday) fires read 19-Aug (Wednesday) as
-prior D1, 1-day gap, expected 1, not stale. But it is the SAME 19-Aug
-D1 bar (`H=13630.10 L=13522.80 C=13602.80`, canonical per the section
-above) that later became stale on 2026-08-21 fires when the 20-Aug
